!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/fixtures/validate-template-family-members.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/40/m/meta.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/40/m/core.tn"
@doc:"""
  A template is not a type, so a family whose members are applications is based on a record ([TSON-SCHEMA] §5.10).
  `boxed` is the abstract base, `box` composes it, and `bt` declares an application of `box`, which IS-A `boxed`
  through `box`'s written parent. A position typed `boxed` dispatches by tag over the declared members.

  An application written at a use site of a template composing no declared type is a type read where it is written:
  `k: plain<text>` is read against `plain<text>`. `shape` states a selector, and `abstract` and a selector on a
  template are each application's, so `s: shape<circle>` is an abstract base whose members would be the declarations
  composing `shape<circle>`, and here there are none.
  """
!schema {
  boxed  => abstract { }
  box    => <T> boxed & { v: T }
  bt     => box<int32>
  plain  => <T> { v: T }
  holder => { any: boxed  k: plain<text> }
  circle => { r: int32 }
  shape  => <T> { kind: text =?  data: T }
  plot   => { s: shape<circle> }
}
